From: mscharged-port
Subject: Draw the Mii icons of the online scenes
Upstream-base: a353c8f2dfb34eb08fecd725965a46ea629428e3
Classification: native admission; the icons draw as on the console.

Patch 0740 admitted the online scenes with MiiManager::CreateIcon returning
false before RFLMakeIcon, so the Mii selection, the hub and the lobby rows
showed empty slots. The online module now compiles RFL_Icon.c and, through
mscharged_add_original_rfl_shape, RFL_MakeTex.c with the transports of the
Mii model's and face texture's Wii-serialized data, so both overloads draw
the icon as the console does: the face texture and model into the EFB, then
GXCopyTex into the icon's own 128x128 RGB5A3 buffer, which Aurora binds when
the icon texture's GXInitTexObj names that buffer.

diff --git a/src/Game/MiiManager.cpp b/src/Game/MiiManager.cpp
index 753d3af..b1030e1 100644
--- a/src/Game/MiiManager.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/MiiManager.cpp
@@ -107,11 +107,6 @@ void MiiManager::LoadResources()
 
 bool MiiManager::CreateIcon(int officialIndex, int iconSlot, RFLExpression expression)
 {
-#if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE) && defined(MSCHARGED_DIAGNOSTIC_FRONTEND_ONLINE)
-    // RFLMakeIcon's GX drawing is not admitted natively yet. Without an icon
-    // the online Mii selection still lists and selects every Mii.
-    return false;
-#endif
     if (officialIndex < 0)
     {
         return false;
@@ -141,11 +136,6 @@ bool MiiManager::CreateIcon(int officialIndex, int iconSlot, RFLExpression expre
 
 bool MiiManager::CreateIcon(const RFLStoreData* data, int iconSlot, RFLExpression expression)
 {
-#if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE) && defined(MSCHARGED_DIAGNOSTIC_FRONTEND_ONLINE)
